    '|a||When did they go home? (разошли́сь: went their ways)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В два часа́ но́чи.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1920
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Together and apart: what do с- and раз- add, with -ся? Посмотри́те. Мно́го однокла́ссников собрало́сь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Однокла́ссник: a classmate, from класс. Собра́ться: to get together.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1g4ihk2'
    '|a||Съе́хались из ра́зных городо́в: they came together from different cities. Ра́зный: different.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ihliib'
    '|a||Мы разошли́сь в два часа́ но́чи: they went apart, each one home.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:kx72qs'
    '|a||С- with -ся: together, to one place. Раз- with -ся: apart, each their own way.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:fi2g72'
    '|a||Шко́ла в Москве́, и ра́зные города́.':
